Docket No. ER26-3380-000 

REQUEST FOR REHEARING OF THE  
INDICATED PJM TRANSMISSION OWNERS 
Pursuant to Federal Power Act (“FPA”) section 313(a)1 and Rule 7132 of the Rules of 
Practice and Procedure of the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (“FERC” or 
“Commission”),3 the Indicated PJM Transmission Owners4 respectfully request rehearing of 
the Commission’s September 29, 2026 order in this proceeding (the “Order”).5   

1  16 U.S.C. § 825l(a).  
2  See 18 C.F.R. § 385.713 (2026). 
3  18 C.F.R. § 385.211 (2026). 
4  The Indicated PJM Transmission Owners are American Transmission Systems, Inc., Mid-
Atlantic Interstate Transmission, LLC, Trans-Allegheny Interstate Line Company, Keystone 
Appalachian Transmission Company, Jersey Central Power & Light Company, Monongahela 
Power Company, and The Potomac Edison Company (collectively, “The FirstEnergy 
Transmission Companies”) and Duquesne Light Company.  The FirstEnergy Transmission 
Companies are separately filing a rehearing request raising other issues.   
5  See PJM Interconnection, L.L.C., 196 FERC ¶ 61,245 (2026) (“Order”).
